      <td class="abe-column-block-padding" id="abe-column-block-c26a34bb-1cfd-48ec-8205-e6c43c88a41a-padding" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; mso-table-lspace: 0pt; mso-table-rspace: 0pt; padding: 5px; border: none;">
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">On behalf of the City of Columbus, applications are now being accepted from Franklin County non-profit organizations qualified and experienced in after school programming to design and deliver, or expand existing after school programming to students in grades sixth through eighth (middle school) for the 2024-2025 school year. </p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Our goal is to ensure all middle school youth have access to high-quality, evidence-based after school opportunities that meet their needs and support their health, development and education. After school programs support social, emotional, cognitive and academic development, reduce risky behaviors, promote physical health and provide a safe and supportive environment for children and youth. Activities youth engage in outside of school hours are critical to their overall development, highlighting the need for quality after school programs in all communities. </p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">The purpose of this Request for Qualifications (RFQ) is to solicit proposals from eligible organizations to design and deliver after school programming in the 2024-2025 school year. Potential program sites could include Columbus City Schools middle school buildings and/or other sites and locations identified by the applicant.  </p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">The application is available through the United Way of Central Ohio’s (UWCO) online proposal submission process. All documents must be submitted through UWCO’s portal, e-CImpact. The deadline for proposal submission is <strong>April 30, 2024 at 5 p.m</strong>. Funding will be available from July 1, 2024 – June 30, 2025.   </p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">To learn more and apply, please click <a href="https://agency.e-cimpact.com/login.aspx?org=37145F&utm_medium=email&utm_source=govdelivery" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #00529B;">here</a>.</p>
<p style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; line-height: 1.4; font-family: helvetica; font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 15px;">Questions? Please contact <a href="mailto:reporting.help@uwcentralohio.org" style="-webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; -ms-text-size-adjust: 100%; color: #00529B;">reporting.help@uwcentralohio.org</a></p>
